# Advanced NLM Configuration Tool
# nlm-config - Command-line configuration management for NLM

**Version 1.0 - Advanced Configuration Management**

This tool provides comprehensive configuration management capabilities for the NLM (Neural Learning Machine) framework. It allows advanced users to:

- Create configuration templates
- Validate and modify configuration files
- Batch process configurations
- Export configurations in multiple formats
- Generate configuration reports
- Apply machine learning-driven configuration optimizations

## Quick Start

```bash
# Create a configuration template
nlm-config init my_project.cfg

# Validate existing configuration
nlm-config validate my_config.cfg

# View configuration details
nlm-config show my_config.cfg

# Modify configuration interactively
nlm-config edit my_config.cfg

# Generate optimized configuration for specific use case
nlm-config optimize learning_config.cfg --target memory

# Export configuration for analysis
nlm-config export learning_config.cfg --format json

# Compare two configurations
nlm-config diff baseline.cfg optimized.cfg

# Apply configuration changes
nlm-config apply optimized.cfg --target brain1

# Batch process multiple configurations
nlm-config batch process *.cfg --output optimized/

# Generate configuration statistics
nlm-config stats learning_config.cfg

# Create configuration template for specific experiment
nlm-config template create memory_learning.cfg --template memory

# Load configuration from database or remote source
nlm-config load database://experiments/v1 --output config.cfg

# Save configuration to database or remote storage
nlm-config save config.cfg database://experiments/v2

# Compare configuration performance metrics
nlm-config benchmark baseline.cfg optimized.cfg --metrics performance
```

## Configuration Formats

### Standard Format (.cfg)
```ini
# NLM Configuration File
# Format: INI-style with support for sections

[basic_settings]
random_seed = 42
simulation_timestep = 0.001
neuron_count = 1000
region_count = 1
connection_probability = 0.1

[learning_parameters]
stdp_ltp_weight = 0.01
stdp_ltd_weight = 0.012
stdp_tau = 20.0

[structural_plasticity]
synaptogenesis_rate = 0.0001
pruning_rate = 0.00001

[memory_system]
working_memory_capacity = 100
max_episodes = 1000

[neuromodulation]
dopamine_level = 0.5
curiosity_drive = 0.3
novelty_threshold = 0.7

[development]
development_rate = 0.1
plasticity_decay = 0.95

[performance]
replay_interval = 100
consolidation_interval = 1000
checkpoint_enabled = true
checkpoint_path = ./checkpoints

[output]
log_level = info
save_stats = true
export_format = binary
```

### JSON Format (.json)
```json
{
  "basic_settings": {
    "random_seed": 42,
    "simulation_timestep": 0.001,
    "neuron_count": 1000,
    "region_count": 1,
    "connection_probability": 0.1
  },
  "learning_parameters": {
    "stdp_ltp_weight": 0.01,
    "stdp_ltd_weight": 0.012,
    "stdp_tau": 20.0
  },
  "structural_plasticity": {
    "synaptogenesis_rate": 0.0001,
    "pruning_rate": 0.00001
  }
}
```

### YAML Format (.yaml)
```yaml
basic_settings:
  random_seed: 42
  simulation_timestep: 0.001
  neuron_count: 1000
  region_count: 1
  connection_probability: 0.1

learning_parameters:
  stdp_ltp_weight: 0.01
  stdp_ltd_weight: 0.012
  stdp_tau: 20.0

structural_plasticity:
  synaptogenesis_rate: 0.0001
  pruning_rate: 0.00001
```

## Command Reference

### nlm-config init
Create a new configuration file with template or defaults.

```bash
# Create basic configuration template
nlm-config init my_config.cfg

# Create specialized configuration template
nlm-config init memory_learning.cfg --template memory

# Create configuration with specific parameters
nlm-config init optimized.cfg --neurons 5000 --max_steps 10000

# Create configuration with file template
nlm-config init project.cfg --template custom_template.ini
```

### nlm-config validate
Validate configuration file syntax and semantics.

```bash
# Validate single configuration file
nlm-config validate my_config.cfg

# Validate all configuration files in directory
nlm-config validate configs/

# Validate with strict mode (prohibit warnings)
nlm-config validate my_config.cfg --strict

# Validate with custom schema
nlm-config validate my_config.cfg --schema brain_schema.json
```

### nlm-config show
Display configuration details and statistics.

```bash
# Show complete configuration
nlm-config show my_config.cfg

# Show only specific sections
nlm-config show my_config.cfg --sections basic_settings learning_parameters

# Show configuration with statistics
nlm-config show my_config.cfg --stats

# Show configuration in specific format
nlm-config show my_config.cfg --format json
```

### nlm-config edit
Edit configuration interactively or programmatically.

```bash
# Edit configuration with text editor
nlm-config edit my_config.cfg

# Edit configuration with programmatic changes
nlm-config edit my_config.cfg --set basic_settings.neuron_count 2000

# Edit multiple parameters
nlm-config edit my_config.cfg \
  --set learning_parameters.stdp_ltp_weight 0.02 \
  --set structural_plasticity.synaptogenesis_rate 0.0002
```

### nlm-config optimize
Generate optimized configuration based on target use case.

```bash
# Optimize for memory learning
nlm-config optimize memory_config.cfg --target memory

# Optimize for development study
nlm-config optimize dev_config.cfg --target development

# Optimize for speed (smaller network)
nlm-config optimize fast_config.cfg --target speed

# Optimize using machine learning
nlm-config optimize ml_config.cfg --target learning --ml-model performance_model.pkl

# Optimize for specific metrics
nlm-config optimize metrics_config.cfg --target memory --metrics episodes learning_rate
```

### nlm-config export
Export configuration to different formats.

```bash
# Export to JSON
nlm-config export config.cfg --format json --output json_config.json

# Export to YAML
nlm-config export config.cfg --format yaml --output yaml_config.yaml

# Export to XML
nlm-config export config.cfg --format xml --output xml_config.xml

# Export with compression
nlm-config export config.cfg --format gzip --output compressed_config.gz

# Export with transformation
nlm-config export config.cfg --format json --transform "scale_neurons 2.0"
```

### nlm-config diff
Compare two configuration files.

```bash
# Simple diff
nlm-config diff baseline.cfg optimized.cfg

# Detailed diff with statistics
nlm-config diff baseline.cfg optimized.cfg --detailed

# Diff with context
nlm-config diff baseline.cfg optimized.cfg --context 5

# Diff specific sections
nlm-config diff baseline.cfg optimized.cfg --sections learning_parameters structural_plasticity
```

### nlm-config apply
Apply configuration changes to target systems.

```bash
# Apply configuration to current brain instance
nlm-config apply config.cfg --target current

# Apply configuration to new brain instance
nlm-config apply config.cfg --target brain1

# Apply configuration with validation
nlm-config apply config.cfg --target brain1 --validate

# Apply multiple configuration files
nlm-config apply config1.cfg config2.cfg config3.cfg --target brain1
```

### nlm-config batch
Process multiple configuration files in batch mode.

```bash
# Process all configurations
nlm-config batch process *.cfg --output processed/

# Batch validate configurations
nlm-config batch validate configs/*.cfg --output validation_report.json

# Batch optimize configurations
nlm-config batch optimize configs/*.cfg --target memory --output optimized/

# Batch export configurations
nlm-config batch export configs/*.cfg --format json --output exports/
```

### nlm-config stats
Generate configuration statistics and analysis.

```bash
# Generate basic statistics
nlm-config stats my_config.cfg

# Generate detailed statistics
nlm-config stats my_config.cfg --detailed

# Generate performance statistics
nlm-config stats my_config.cfg --metrics performance

# Generate memory statistics
nlm-config stats my_config.cfg --metrics memory

# Generate statistics report
nlm-config stats my_config.cfg --format json --output stats.json
```

### nlm-config template
Create and manage configuration templates.

```bash
# Create predefined template
nlm-config template create memory_learning.cfg --template memory

# Create custom template
nlm-config template create my_template.cfg --name "My Custom Template"

# List available templates
nlm-config template list

# Load template
nlm-config template load memory_learning.cfg

# Save template
nlm-config template save my_template.cfg
```

### nlm-config benchmark
Run benchmarks on configurations.

```bash
# Benchmark configuration performance
nlm-config benchmark config.cfg --metrics performance memory

# Compare multiple configurations
nlm-config benchmark config1.cfg config2.cfg config3.cfg --metrics all

# Run benchmark with simulation
nlm-config benchmark config.cfg --simulate --duration 1000

# Generate benchmark report
nlm-config benchmark config.cfg --format json --output benchmark.json
```

### nlm-config load / nlm-config save
Load and save configurations from/to external sources.

```bash
# Load configuration from database
nlm-config load database://experiments/v1 --output config.cfg

# Load configuration from remote URL
nlm-config load https://example.com/config.json --output config.json

# Save configuration to database
nlm-config save config.cfg database://experiments/v2

# Save configuration to remote URL
nlm-config save config.json https://example.com/config.json

# Load/save with authentication
nlm-config load remote://user:pass@host/config.cfg --output config.cfg
```

