## Installation and Usage

### System Requirements
- C++17 or higher
- CMake 3.16 or higher
- Python 3.8 or higher (for ML integration)
- pip packages: numpy, scikit-learn, keras/tensorflow (optional)

### Build Instructions
```bash
# Clone repository
cd /path/to/nlm
cmake -B build -H.
make -C build -j4

# Install
make install -C build
```

### Quick Start Script
```bash
#!/bin/bash

# Quick start configuration setup

echo "Setting up NLM configuration..."

# Create project directory
mkdir -p nlm_projects/my_project/configs
mkdir -p nlm_projects/my_project/checkpoints
mkdir -p nlm_projects/my_project/exports

# Initialize main configuration
nlm-config init nlm_projects/my_project/configs/main.cfg

# Create specialized configurations
nlm-config template create nlm_projects/my_project/configs/memory.cfg --template memory
nlm-config template create nlm_projects/my_project/configs/development.cfg --template development

# Validate configurations
nlm-config validate nlm_projects/my_project/configs/*.cfg

# Generate report
nlm-config stats nlm_projects/my_project/configs/main.cfg --format json > nlm_projects/my_project/analysis/main_stats.json

echo "Configuration setup complete!"
echo "You can now run NLM experiments using configurations in nlm_projects/my_project/configs/"
```

